## Helper Binaries

Cursor ships 3 helper binaries in `resources/helpers/`:

| Binary | Size | Purpose |
|--------|------|---------|
| `crepectl.exe` | ~10MB | Chrome DevTools Protocol controller — how Cursor controls the Chromium browser engine for webviews |
| `cursorsandbox.exe` | ~5MB | Sandboxed execution environment — provides process isolation for sensitive operations |
| `node.exe` | ~40MB | Bundled Node.js runtime — Cursor's own Node.js build, not system-installed |

### crepectl.exe

Controls Chrome DevTools Protocol connections for webview management. Used by:
- Webview content rendering
- CDP-based debugging
- Browser automation
- Webview lifecycle management

### cursorsandbox.exe

Provides an isolated execution environment. Used for:
- Running untrusted code in isolated processes
- Sandboxed terminal sessions
- Agent command execution isolation

### node.exe

Cursor bundles its own Node.js runtime (typically a specific version) rather than relying on system Node.js. This ensures:
- Consistent behavior across environments
- No version conflicts with user-installed Node.js
- Bundled with specific dependencies needed by Cursor's extensions

