## ASAR Archive

Cursor bundles all Node.js dependencies into an ASAR archive:

| File | Size | Purpose |
|------|------|---------|
| `node_modules.asar` | 28 bytes (metadata) | Bundled dependencies in ASAR format |

The ASAR archive contains all `node_modules` dependencies bundled into a single archive file for:
- Faster startup (fewer files to stat)
- Reduced disk I/O
- Simplified distribution

Dependencies packed in the ASAR include:
- `@connectrpc/connect` (gRPC-Web for agent communication)
- `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` v1.25.1 (MCP protocol)
- `better-sqlite3` (agent state store)
- `tree-sitter` (syntax-aware code analysis)
- `@anysphere/tree-chunk-napi` (Rust code chunking)
- `esbuild` / `esbuild-wasm` (bundler)
- `zod` v4 (validation schemas)
- `node-ignore` (.gitignore parsing)
- `dompurify` (HTML sanitization)
- And thousands of transitive dependencies

